anSA" style=3D"color: #0077B6;">belligerent denial</a> through your proxies=
.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">The fourth stage? We=E2=80=99ll know soon =
enough.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Within the last month, we have traipsed, o=
n tiptoes, into a strange new age where some modicum of repercussion may oc=
casionally threaten the billionaire class =E2=80=93 albeit strictly limited=
 to the confines of sports, where nothing actually matters. It=E2=80=99s a =
new and funny feeling in an age when it seems that the 1% don=E2=80=99t jus=
t get a bespoke business climate, where taxation and regulation are adminis=
tered on an opt-in basis, but their own concierge service from the justice =
system, too.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Setting aside for the moment the argument =
of whether billionaires should exist at all, or whether they are a flagrant=
 failure of fiscal policy, this is a remarkable turn of events.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">On 2 September, the NBA released the findi=
ngs of an investigation: The Los Angeles Clippers and their owner Steve Bal=
lmer were officially caught paying star forward Kawhi Leonard $28m off the =
books for a no-show job with a supposed sponsor, circumventing the league=
=E2=80=99s salary cap. The Clippers were <a href=3D"https://ablink.editoria=
l.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IRyTNtZQ7fIEMgszcCSneHEDlPW9=
baUaXg5N4KmoOwCw6TFDfrOX__sAU2sCma3_9XWX5prCnJsjXLpJ63xX2ClWn_4SVbGGwOpvMf1=
UDXeCFvOS5Ph-W1ksjKVQ6yKmZwgA5iXaCDzxVmac7W3KgKRI-d9E86oRl36x_PpYZcJfcGwp0e=
HJGdGNEIv_E98_5L5WM11qYQ3qNn_XySmsU2PmAiZ5Wt3VvJegBmwstPSMCJzZJZXXvKLW8R4fj=
krcZaWeuCRRucEvmd6mRJi9seMbicy5JvJM2dXxxlH55_4HShK3uRFJE1aVOvtPVBJ6bsw/4ui/=
epM9dszhSn2jEmhms0MiXw/h24/h001.fwjOub4sHJ1Wz0N87uKiSyhzJZaB8bW_g-qqpxeJwdE=
" style=3D"color: #0077B6;">docked five first-round picks and fined $30m</a=
>. Ballmer, the ninth richest man in the world, was suspended from involvem=
ent with his team for a year. Initially, the Clippers <a href=3D"https://ab=
link.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IRyQGjQE3QcuuP9=
9JhdZ4fBHEiidQ1INFnQR0ru0GLy0vtjcxyyXpIZ1HwcpwSxVofm7jQC2F8AGjGmGGbWeOeGiG7=
Na9Rt_z6N7y3x8ZgM6gksWI4hjovvrg6bD9r_B5-S8VPhmZjFabcLzlo_Ps7cfmOvBRRH3T0Ylt=
WUb0eAedIWOWv-HNBFadOsnm_e9BQuAqnBdCoEswVNcgAt9h3cOlns7VI1lMEcrjcbnzg1zaQrW=
BUs6FhKDLD7L6Mhq-Fx9CVDcXqshxxdWOYU4npEHe6ZOftj7AaHwGniRcmZjueBvvMyxi2JPu-4=
Ev2ugscQ/4ui/epM9dszhSn2jEmhms0MiXw/h25/h001.qY5r7jYUvV9XfwRvJy7aDKTxYS49tE=
8BWfjVb64yd0Q" style=3D"color: #0077B6;">issued a statement</a>, snarling t=
hat they =E2=80=9Cvehemently reject the NBA=E2=80=99s findings, which are t=
he result of a heavily biased investigation seeking to justify a predetermi=
ned narrative rather than facts and evidence=E2=80=9D.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Then, the team accepted the punishment.</p=
