 our Monday edition of the newsletter.</em></p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;"><strong>Thursday:</strong> The hiring of J=
=C3=BCrgen Klopp was supposed to revitalize a Germany side that has disappo=
inted at the past two World Cups. It hasn=E2=80=99t quite worked out like t=
hat, After a shocking loss to Greece in the Nations League, Germany needs p=
oints against Serbia in Munich. <em><strong style=3D"color: #0077B6; font-s=
tyle: normal; font-weight: 700;">Germany v Serbia</strong></em> kicks off a=
t 2.45pm on Fox Soccer Plus and Vix.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;"><strong>Friday:</strong> It=E2=80=99s a re=
match of the 2006 World Cup final, a battle between one of Europe=E2=80=99s=
 best teams and one of its most disappointing, and just generally a stone-c=
old classic. France v Italy kicks off at 2.45pm on FS1. (If you have time t=
o witness history, tune in to <em><strong style=3D"color: #0077B6; font-sty=
le: normal; font-weight: 700;">Seattle Reign v North Carolina Courage</stro=
ng></em> at 10pm on NWSL+ too =E2=80=93 Courage attacker Ashley Sanchez can=
 break the NWSL=E2=80=99s single-season scoring record with a goal)</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;"><strong>Saturday:</strong> If there=E2=80=
=99s one truism of American soccer it=E2=80=99s this: USA v Mexico always d=
elivers. The latest chapter in the storied and heated rivalry will focus on=
 the next generation of young players who populate both squads. <em><strong=
 style=3D"color: #0077B6; font-style: normal; font-weight: 700;">USA v Mexi=
co</strong></em> kicks off at 10pm on TNT and Telemundo.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;"><strong>Sunday:</strong> How will Portugal=
 get on without Cristiano Ronaldo, who left the team=E2=80=99s camp on Wedn=
esday? We=E2=80=99ll get a better idea in the team=E2=80=99s last game of t=
his long international window, hosting Erling Haaland and Norway in Porto. =
<em><strong style=3D"color: #0077B6; font-style: normal; font-weight: 700;"=
